+## Forward V13: one paused recorder fence, then original Stop
+
+Prepared 2026-11-05 in a private directory only, from all six reconstructed and
+byte-verified V12 postimages. No candidate import, SQL, Docker, test, credential,
+provider, hosted or repository mutation was performed. The V12 raw result and
+review bundles remain unchanged. This is a new held-source closed laboratory
+candidate, not a hosted migration or source-adoption decision.
+
+### Exact additional transition
+
+`installation -> [one fence_acquire] -> source_stop`; no other operation is
+admitted. Acquire is restricted to position 2, paused mode, the original
+installed acquisition epoch, no held fence and revision zero. The real scoped
+recorder must have `fence_manage` and match the installed recorder binding;
+control/installer/reader or a foreign recorder cannot substitute an ID. The
+closed four-field acquire body requests exactly the decimal string `60000000`
+microseconds. Both expected-fence fields remain null in this slice; the exact
+previous HeadPin and installed no-fence state still bind admission.
+
+The operation and fence IDs are distinct fresh UUIDs with original allocation
+associations and separate `native_operation_id`/`fence_id` records. Both the
+scope-local precheck and original global unique indexes reject reused IDs. The
+source checks the original installation by the existing complete committed
+prefix verifier before minting the server-held fence. It writes the exact
+nine-field FenceRecord from the earlier lifecycle proposal and its distinct
+original pin. No caller can provide revision, issue/expiry time, or receipt.
+The issued time is sampled after locked validation; final-function observation
+is sampled after staging. The deferred guard reauthorizes the actual recorder,
+rederives the exact staged fence and both identity rows, checks the locked
+prior head and all existing budget/session conditions, then samples recognized
+COMMIT processing. Require `issued <= final <= commit < expires` and exactly
+60 seconds from issue to expiry; equality at expiry refuses. These are actual
+uncalibrated database observations, not a hard final-visible/WAL freshness or
+production clock claim. No test waits for expiry or alters a clock.
+
+Result and getter keep the pinned closed wire types. Acquire has five distinct
+direct pins (three installed facts, installation Command, exact new fence) and
+seven getter pins (three installed facts, fence and installation C/R/T). The
+verifier independently reconstructs the closed record/clock/identity associations
+from the exact originals, held epoch and bound writer in its one parent-statement
+snapshot; historical installation readback does not include later fence pins.
+Two table CHECK unions admit the new action and domain fact. The remaining
+function inventory, broker, roles, grants, exact source-loader contract,
+policy bytes, fixture constructor/catalog checks and public entries stay fixed.
+
+### Terminal path and accounting
+
+Admitting a fence while retaining V12's no-fence-only Stop would strand the
+reserved operation. This increment therefore accepts the original reserved Stop
+at position 3 against the exact committed acquire, its active fence ID/epoch and
+current head. Stop remains paused-to-stopped and does not require a live hold.
+It clears active fence and increments revision once; retained originals/identity/
+fence facts remain intact. Direct Stop pins number six (three installed facts,
+installation Command, acquire Command, retained fence); getter closure is ten
+(two ancestor C/R/T trios plus four domain facts). The V12 four-direct/six-closure
+no-fence Stop remains available after installation. This does not exercise an
+expired held-fence Stop, seven direct pins, or complete reserve liveness.
+
+The generic selected final/pending representation still charges each actual C/R,
+Receipt/Journal/head/accounting/metadata occurrence and every declared logical
+key; pending original and deferred update are separately charged. Acquire's
+ScopeHead upper envelope now holds a full UUID instead of null (34 more bytes
+in that component), only for acquire; existing install/Stop costs retain their
+shape. The maximum revision in this narrow path is two, so the existing two-digit
+upper width is conservative. The prior private November worksheet identified
+conditional full-seven-pin bounds but does not authorize wider source semantics
+or changes to the issued reserve constants. Existing logical/staging byte caps,
+position and Stop reserve checks stay fixed. Derived row/key touches are not
+physical PostgreSQL tuple/index/TOAST/WAL measurements.
+
+Hand ledger for the new three-operation path (including six bootstrap rows):
+
+| Operation | New retained rows | Final logical writes/keys | DML/key touches incl. staging |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Installation | 23 | 24 / 48 | 25 / 51 |
+| Acquire | 10 | 11 / 22 | 12 / 25 |
+| Stop with retained fence | 8 | 9 / 18 | 10 / 21 |
+| Total | 47 retained including bootstrap | 44 / 88 | 47 / 97 |
+
+Five additional native methods check actual clock/record/active-head/pin/encoded
+readback and independent selected row/key charges; non-recorder, foreign and
+closed-body refusal; fresh ID collision, stale/second acquire and original
+conflict; provisional rollback/early-trigger refusal and preserved terminal
+reserve; and complete original Stop-with-fence/readback/replay/no new fact state.
+The original 24 methods remain; exactly one method removes now-implemented
+`fence_acquire` from its unsupported-kind list. No other original method body
+changes. New code uses no artificial sleep or enlarged timeout.
+
+### Review and execution boundary
+
+All 29 unique tests, including the unchanged first statistics method in the
+same position, require a separately reviewed complete current-base snapshot and
+root-owned bounded runner. Keep the existing 240-second whole-module external
+bound, owned cached pinned PG17 image, network none and exact cleanup; no
+candidate runner is invoked here. The actual native test result is unknown.
+Do not infer SQL compilation, fixture constructor/catalog acceptance, sustained
+clock/expiry behavior, Resume/renew/release, other allocator kinds, complete
+seven-pin/capacity witness, production NOLOGIN-owner privileges, runtime
+adoption, worker readiness or live authority from static source preparation.
+
+## Forward V14: keep the source paused after fence acquisition
+
+Independent static review refused V13 before execution: the deferred commit
+guard built the next source mode as paused only for installation. Its fallback
+would mark a committed fence acquisition stopped, contradicting the admitted
+acquire result and preventing the original reserved Stop from using the held
+fence. V14 changes that one CASE to make only source_stop stopped. The already
+admitted installation and fence_acquire actions stay paused. No admission,
+expiry, accounting, getter, broker, ACL, or test change follows from this repair.
+
+The held SQL source changes from `cc4c1425de5035e0fd3b2e6c7dec40b90a06068b9795703fe7dd267e74dedea9`
+to `9d0e2b94f45919e0a734c0df1f72826068f60c9248d819a8d2d9de27a7fdbb1e`; the fixture source pin follows. All 29 test methods are
+byte-identical to V13. V13 remains frozen and unexecuted. This V14 candidate is
+also unexecuted and pending independent review and exact current-base composition.
